  "summary": "Neon bombshells, chrome futures and monster mashes painted on glass behind flashing lights.",
  "description": "Pinball's backglass and playfield art is a 90-year commercial illustration tradition: Airbrushed starlets, hot rods, devils, spacemen and, since the 1990s, licensed movie and band themes — painted by house artists like Gordon Morison, Dave Christensen (Firepower), Pat McMahon and Python Anghelo, with playfields adding ramps, plastics and pop bumpers as physical set-dressing. Machines like The Addams Family (1992) and medieval Madness merged theme, humor and layout into cult canon; collectors restore glasses under UV light, and modern Stern machines keep commissioning full illustrated packages. It is vernacular American illustration at arcade scale.",
  "culturalContext": "Pinball art is 90 years of American commercial illustration at arcade scale: backglass painters shaped taste alongside movie posters, the collector restoration scene (IPDB documentation, UV restoration) treats glasses as fine print artifacts, and Stern's licensed machines keep the illustrated-package tradition commercially alive.",
